<article class="env-remark" id="0BBL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BBL">Remark <span data-tag="0BBL">66.7.6</span>.</a> Let $P$ be a property of local rings. Assume that for any étale ring map $A \to B$ and $\mathfrak q$ is a prime of $B$ lying over the prime $\mathfrak p$ of $A$, then $P(A_\mathfrak p) \Leftrightarrow P(B_\mathfrak q)$. Then we obtain an étale local property of germs $(U, u)$ of schemes by setting $\mathcal{P}(U, u) = P(\mathcal{O}_{U, u})$. In this situation we will use the terminology “the local ring of $X$ at $x$ has $P$” to mean $X$ has property $\mathcal{P}$ at $x$. Here is a list of such properties $P$: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Noetherian, see More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AGZ" data-tag="0AGZ">15.45.1</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
dimension $d$, see More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/07QP" data-tag="07QP">15.45.2</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
regular, see More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AH0" data-tag="0AH0">15.45.3</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
discrete valuation ring, follows from (2), (3), and Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00PD" data-tag="00PD">10.119.7</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
reduced, see More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/06DH" data-tag="06DH">15.46.4</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
normal, see More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/06DI" data-tag="06DI">15.46.6</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Noetherian and depth $k$, see More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/06LL" data-tag="06LL">15.46.8</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Noetherian and Cohen-Macaulay, see More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/06LM" data-tag="06LM">15.46.9</a>, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Noetherian and Gorenstein, see Dualizing Complexes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BJL" data-tag="0BJL">47.21.9</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> There are more properties for which this holds, for example G-ring and Nagata. If we every need these we will add them here as well as references to detailed proofs of the corresponding algebra facts. </p>
